    "standardized_narrative": "Opening gross claims outstanding at 1 January 2021 were GBP 722.4m. During 2021 there was an adverse prior-year run-off (strengthening) of GBP 32.2m, primarily driven by catastrophe-related adverse development (notably Hurricane Laura and the 2010 New Zealand Earthquake) together with other prior-year large loss development. Current-year catastrophe events (Winter Storm Uri, European Floods, Hurricane Ida, US Tornados and Amplify Energy) materially impacted the current accident year loss ratio but the explicit prior year reserve movement disclosed is a GBP 32.2m strengthening (approx. 4.46% of opening gross claims outstanding).",
